#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:41
#. Diagram label
msgid "Agents stalled, owner asks to pick up work, or agent re-enters"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:42
#. Diagram label
msgid "Audit remote delta, epic relay snapshot & PR classes"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:24
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Audits remote default-branch and beans deltas, reads the epic write-ahead Live Relay Snapshot, classifies open and draft PRs, inspects worktrees, /tmp overlays, and Cargo/Lean donor caches non-destructively (rescuing dirty stalled work onto claude/salvage-* rather than resetting), consolidates themes, and reconciles the epic lease table."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:57
#. Diagram label
msgid "Consolidate into 2-4 themes, with a recommendation each"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:61
#. Diagram label
msgid "Decide each theme"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:37
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Decides one theme at a time (continue, fold into the plan, new epic, park, or scrap), or supplies standing grant/plan continuity when returning on a turn without scope ambiguity."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:73
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Green ready-to-merge PRs join the Merge Steward queue; active external sibling drafts stay untouched; mid-merge or salvaged stalled branches are re-driven cleanly from their PR or salvage head; owner-fenced PRs hold."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:58
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Group by what the work delivers, not by agent. Each theme gets its epic, members, dependencies, risk, and one of: continue, fold in, new epic, park, scrap (owner only)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:49
#. Diagram label
msgid "Inspect worktrees non-destructively, salvage & collect handovers"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:32
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge steward"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:72
#. Diagram label
msgid "Re-route ready PRs & resume Merge Steward + worker queues"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:33
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Receives classified open PRs: queues verified green ready-to-merge PRs, leaves active external sibling drafts untouched, re-drives mid-merge or stalled branches from their PR head or salvage branch, and holds owner-fenced PRs."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:64
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reconcile epic lease table, write-ahead checkpoint & sibling notes"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:79
#. Diagram label
msgid "Relay reconciled; queues and epic lease table live"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:17
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled-agent triage & bidirectional relay re-entry"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:15
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled-agent triage & bidirectional relay re-entry: audit deltas, salvage worktrees, consolidate, re-route"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:50
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Step 4 of re-entry reconciliation: inspect every local worktree (git status --short --branch, ahead/behind origin), /tmp overlays, and Cargo/Lean donor caches without ever running git reset --hard; rescue dirty or unpushed stalled work onto a claude/salvage-* branch (and push it) or resume in place, and verify or reconstruct handover reports. Unpushed remote state is unknown, never empty."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:65
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Step 5 of re-entry reconciliation: update and push the epic bean's write-ahead Worktree/Branch/Scratch Lease Table, child beans, and active/excluded hypotheses on cat/cat-harness/beans; record a 'triage: <date>' note, claim picked-up work via beans:claim, and post sibling coordination notes if landed commits shifted scope."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:43
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Steps 1-3 of re-entry reconciliation: fetch origin/<default-branch> and origin/cat/cat-harness/beans, audit git log <last-known-sha>..origin/<default-branch>, read the epic bean's write-ahead Live Relay Snapshot (child beans, active research/compute hypotheses, negative/excluded routes, lease table), and classify open and draft PRs into ready-to-merge, active external sibling draft, stalled with uncommitted/unpushed work, and owner-fenced."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:23
#. Diagram label
msgid "Triage / re-entering agent"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:36
#. Diagram label
msgid "User"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:18
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "When agents stall (quota exhausted, context full, container lost, session timed out) OR when an agent returns on its next turn after another session advanced the repository, execute Bidirectional Relay Continuity: reconcile remote commits and epic write-ahead snapshots, classify open and draft PRs, inspect worktrees, /tmp overlays, and Cargo/Lean donor caches non-destructively (never git reset --hard; rescue dirty unpushed work onto claude/salvage-* or resume in place), consolidate workstreams into 2-4 themes when owner triage is needed, reconcile the epic lease table on cat/cat-harness/beans, and re-route ready PRs through the Merge Steward. Operating skills: stalled-agent-triage, handover-report, prepare-for-handover, agent-handoff, bean-coordination, coordinate, merge-manager-watcher."
msgstr ""
